







Update only the existing real TestNG 7.12.0
integration test where an independent ITestListener
attempts to read invocation-scoped configuration.

The current architecture guarantees an active
INVOCATION context for coordinator-managed callbacks,
not for independently registered TestNG listeners.

Requirements:

1. Preserve the independent ITestListener.

2. Verify its onTestSuccess receives the correct
   INVOCATION UUID through ITestResult attributes.

3. Verify the independent listener does not
   automatically receive an active ScopeCursor binding.

4. Add or reuse a coordinator-managed onTestSuccess
   callback in the same integration test.

5. Verify the managed callback receives the correct
   active INVOCATION UUID.

6. Verify it reads the override created by
   the test body through the normal configuration API.

7. Verify temporary activation cleanup.

8. Verify the invocation is released after
   the owning TestNG context finishes.

9. Do not depend on the callback registration order
   of independent listeners.

10. Do not modify production code or other tests.

11. Do not weaken UUID, configuration isolation
    or lifecycle safety assertions.

Run only this integration test and report
the exact result.
